Subject: [PATCH] Lock-chat app-state event and media transfers with progress
 and cancel

The changes of the neonize test build 0.5.2-winzapp-teste.2 (fork
reffehcsoibaf/neonize, branch feat/group-request-participants; upstream
pull requests krypton-byte/neonize #227 to #232), merged upstream in neonize 0.8.0 (events 46-49 and 51-53, fetch_app_state,
request_app_state_recovery, the PatchInfo fix, update_group_request_participants).
What 0.8.0 lacks stays here, rebased on 0.10.0:

- the lock-chat app-state event (50);
- download to and upload from disk with progress and cancel.

Original description (0.6.0):

- app-state events from the phone: archive, pin, mute, mark-as-read,
  lock, delete chat, delete-for-me and star (events 46 to 53);
- fetch_app_state and request_app_state_recovery;
- DecodePatchInfo maps PatchInfo.Type to the right collection;
- download to and upload from disk with progress and cancel;
- update_group_request_participants.

Generated code (Neonize.pb.go, Neonize_pb2.py/.pyi) is not part of the
patch: build_neonize.py regenerates it from Neonize.proto.
